>>>Is it possible to use a HP DS20 firmware upgrade, or will this not work?  

>> Not DS20, but probably DS20L


> If I try it, I will post the results ;)

> Paul

OK, for the people who are interested...  I tried it..  And I advise you 
not to try it! Unless you have plenty time, and don't mind to sweat a bit 
.. ;-)   

What I did is the following;

- I downloaded the latest firmware for the DS20L from HP's ftp site (The 
link at the firmware page didn't work anymore...)
- I installed a tftp server at my other linux box, and dumped the .exe 
file from HP in there..
- I configured the ethernet adapter in SRM to boot the file from that 
other box..
- I booted the file, and upgraded the SRM.  However, and this is the 
tricky part (I think), there was NO diags firmware shipped with the SRM 
update. So I had the old diags firmware with a new SRM.
- After the restart of the CS20, it looked like it was working..  It 
showed hp DS20L as identifier..  But that was the first and last time it 
worked..  Booting into aboot was no problem, but booting the kernel just 
stopped after "uncompressing kernel image" ..
- After restarting (power off / power on) the box, it didn't come past the 
message "Entering main diags kernel" ..  It just locked up!



- I cleared the NVRAM, using jumper 1-2 (see docs for this), and entered 
some default values. (like console settings)
- After entering the settings I exited to the SRM console.  This worked.. 
(lucky me!)

The next steps took me about 3 hours to figure out...

- I made a API Networks firmware CD (ISO available at www.alphalinux.org )
- I copied all the files from the Options directory to the root of the CD
- I started up lfu from the SRM console
- Waited till the search was complete, and entered as device name where 
the ROM images could be found "dqb1.1.1.16.0"
- Entered as file list "cs20fw.txt"  (IMPORTANT!!  It searches for a 
"ds20lfw.txt", since it is programmed as a DS20L at that moment!)
- LFU read all the files, and I used the update option.
- Rebooted the system, with still the nvram jumper installed. Entered some 
settings, powered the system off, removed the jumper, and powered on 
again.

That was it!

I was back at the place where I started.. Everthing was working again like 
before.. :-)

I will give it another shot if I ever get an DS20L firmware with all the 
ROMS included (SROM/PAL/SRM/DIAG). But if one of those is missing I am not 
trying it anymore!


Paul Zwierstra
pzw1@xs4all.nl


PS I will make a nice webpage about this when I am finished with 
everything, so everybody who's in the same situation can read all about it :).


