ben_myers@charter.net (Ben Myers) writes:

>Rich,

>Matrox card have alaways had a high degree of backward compatibility.  The G200
>should work just fine.  A G400 has pretty good odds, too... Ben Myers

plus AGP 2X is backwards compatible.  you can in fact use a AGP 4X or 8X capable
card in a AGP 1X slot.  so it actually doesn't really matter what sort of card
you buy except for trying to avoid cards which are power hogs and might draw
too much power across the AGP bus which can cause system issues, especially
under windows which can be somewhat sensitive (and cryptic) in dealing with such.

if the person is planning on gaming they should look at XP pro since that will
use both cpus (obviously not in a non multithreaded game, but perhaps one for
system stuff and the other for the game itself) and has the most up to date
support for mid-range/older cards.

i'd probably recommend he look at a gf2 or gf3, or alternately a radeon 7500 or
8500LE, but really any mid to low end peecee video card would probably be fine
and faster than what he has now.

cheers,

-jason


