Jeff et al,

Some AGP cards are made for dual use.  Attach an NLX mounting bracket and they
satisfy the physical requirements for mounting in an NLX chassis.  Attach a
standard mounting bracket and they fit a standard ATX chassis.

In my experience, certain models of Matrox, ATI, Elsa (RIP), and Number Nine
(RIP #2) cards are designed to fit either NLX or ATX.  All you need is a bracket
with the opening for the external monitor connector lined up at the right
height.  ALL?  Actually, switching cards back and forth between NLX and ATX is
not too easy.

Matrox, ATI, Elsa, and Number Nine are/were OEM suppliers to name-brand players
who built NLX or NLX-like systems: DEC, Compaq, IBM, and maybe a couple of
others.

eBay has people selling NLX cards from time to time.  I have a few here myself,
should anyone need to buy... Ben Myers

