"Jerome H. Fine" wrote:

> Is there any reasonably easy and simple way to recover the bad blocks.

The problem is almost always head alignment. The RK05 doesn't read servo
info
from the disk, but rather uses dead reckoning with head movement.
Temperature
has some effects, so try it when the drive is cold, or try cooling (not
below
the dew point) or heading the pack.

You could mess about with the head alignment, but have to realign it
again. Plus
you can only adjust the heads out, then have to push them back with you
finger.

Are all the bad blocks only on one surface (ie block number divided by
12 is
always even or odd)


