Be careful before reading RK05 disks the first time after a long period.
There will always be a very fine layer of dust on them, even if they had
been kept in a dust "free" environment. So I open them first and clean the
surfaces with a leave of strong kitchen paper and alcohol (ethanol or
isopropyl). If you don't do that, you will get that "no good" noises out of
the drive and you have to clean the heads and disks. Btw. cleaning the disk
is quite easy: take a Q-tip with alcohol and rub (with a certain force)
until the dark brown "scratches" will disappear. This helped me in bringing
a PDP8 cobol disk back to life with no read errors at all, the disk was
nearly unreadable before.

Christian


