were pulled and pitched (apparently), and along the way they lost the
manuals too.  I located a user manual online that has a lot of info,
but have a problem since battery config and wiring info is not
supplied.

The UPS has three wires to attach the batteries; a large red female
spade, large black female spade, and a small (20 gauge?) grey female
spade tie-wrapped to the black ground lead.  According to the various
battery vendors this unit takes two 12V 7AH batteries, and based on
the one listing I found, the internal power bus should be 24 volts, so
they should be in series.  I can make a jumper wire easily enough,
but... whats that third wire for?  There are no visible male spades on
the frame, on the battery housing, or anywhere else.  Do these units
use batteries with an additional connector?  That might explain the
$40+ price per battery that I've seen.  I don't want to spend almost
$100 on batteries till I know how to wire these beasts up.

Thanks for any assistance.  If I can get these running I can keep them
for home use, and they are supposed to be good quality, smart, true
sine-wave units so worth saving if feasible.

Rich Jordan


