Hi,

I just bought on Ebay a TK50Z-GA which is a tabletop TK50 with a
SCSI-to-TK50-bus converter and a powersupply in one portable
housing. Very nice unit indeed. However... This seems to be a
US-only unit that is specified for a 110 vac suppley only. As our
local powercompany supplies only 230 vac, I have and would like
to do some adaption.

So I disassembled this unit and I found a H7848-BA ps that was
made in Hong Kong. That gave me some hope, they have in Hong Kong
also 220 vac, isn't it? After a brief investigation of the
regulator board inside the ps-housing I think this is a primary
switched PS. It has the assy nr. 70-22655-03 E02. Basicalley this
one should also eat 220 vac and I think that I see a jumper near
the auxilary-x-former that might be there to connect the input
power to the 220 vac tap of this x-former.

Does anyone know this PS? 
What is the function of the jumper? 
Who knows a source for the tech. manual and/or engineering
drawings?
Does there exist a 220 vac variant of this PS?

Electricalley between the PS and the Converterboard there is a
"Loads-board" nr. 5017162-01-A1 that containd 27 5-watt
powerresistors that may be used to "regulate" some voltage by
dissipation. Anyway this board shows by its brown colour below
the resistors that it got pretty hot. This makes me think that
the converter-board uses a different voltage as the H7848 does
suppley. The number on the SCSI-to-TK50-bus converter board is:
5017638-01-B1-P2 and the firmware in EPROM reads
DEC90LM9042453E6.

Does anyone have info on this converterboard, especialley on its
power-requirements and its functional specifications?

The seccond best solution would be providing another PS that
supplies the required power for the TK50 and the converterboard.
Does anyone know the required voltages and power dissipation for
these?

Thanks in avance for your help

Frank


