They are connected to a cat 5000 on the FDDI ring and off of the cat
there are Ethernet machines bridged/switched on the same "network".
When hosts with Ethernet need to communicate with those with FDDI, it
is slow as heck for NFS.  I am thinking that it is an MTU issue.  I
would like to try to change the MTU on the DEC Ultrix hosts.  Newer
os's, like Linux and Dec Unix have MTU adjustability via ifconfig.  The
old fashioned way I would do this kinda thing would be via adb and
dynamicly updating the MTU size in the running kernel.  Or updating it
in the vmunix file prior to boot.

I am looking to see if anyone knows these locations so I can poke into
the memory/vmunix and update the value.  I hope this is possible.  I
would even me up for building kernels that have a 1500byte FDDI MTU.  But
w/o source, it is not easy to know what locations to update.

