Frank Arnold wrote:
> 

> So I disassembled this unit and I found a  ps that was
> made in Hong Kong. That gave me some hope, they have in Hong Kong
> also 220 vac, isn't it? After a brief investigation of the
> regulator board inside the ps-housing I think this is a primary
> switched PS. It has the assy nr. 70-22655-03 E02. Basicalley this
> one should also eat 220 vac and I think that I see a jumper near
> the auxilary-x-former that might be there to connect the input
> power to the 220 vac tap of this x-former.
> 

A H7848-BB for 220V has the jumper exactly in the opposite position,
next to the rectifier. This seems to be a common theme of switched power
supplies in the years before '90 or so, in that many of them were
designed for international use and just required a jumper to switch the
primary circuit from simple bridge rectifier for 220Vac to a voltage
doubler for 110Vac. That's also the reason why there are two
eltctrolytic caps of the same capacitance, but rather low voltage
(200Vdc), which are put in series for 220Vac.
A DECServer 100 has the same setup.


