In article <f9ca1551.0210021947.696daa7c@posting.google.com>, jwillis@arielusa.com (John Willis) writes:
>Replacing the "T" connector results in a change in error 
>message from 0011.700E to 0000.7004

According to the manual, 0000.7004 indicates: Not connected to Thin-Wire
ethernet.

I'd suggest that you check the T connector and both terminators you have
on that connector.  If you have a DVM, check that the terminators have a
resistance of 50 ohms and with both connected to the T you should see a
resistance of 25 ohms.  

